0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Action: Run the PBM fiduciary checklist on a recurring cycle and keep the output for the six-year lookback.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Detail: Send a CAA letter on consultant compensation, audit rebates and spread pricing, and review the formulary and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (MAC pricing [Frier Levitt - jpLEKhmPpLs @ 00:44:54]. Pair that with training, delegation, documentation, audits,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (market checks, RFP/RFI work and identification of every vendor fee [Seyfarth Shaw LLP - EwDJFTGZkoE @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (00:58:07].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (The money mechanics start with how PBMs actually get paid. Ben at Seyfarth Shaw walks through the models. Spread) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (pricing means the PBM buys at $10 and sells to the plan at $20. Pass-through pricing adds a per-employee-per-month) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (fee. Then there is rebate retention, plus the less visible cuts from pharmacy ownership and shared-savings arrangements) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm ([EwDJFTGZkoE @ 00:27:30]. Frier Levitt's panel names the current profit engine: generics relabeled as specialty) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (drugs. Those drugs are reimbursed at AWP minus 12 percent instead of AWP minus 87 percent on molecules that cost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm ($1 to $3 a pill, and exclusivity is steered to PBM-owned specialty pharmacies [jpLEKhmPpLs @ 00:09:14]. Mike Hill) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (gives the headline number from the J&J complaint. Teriflunomide carries an average pharmacy acquisition cost of 91) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (cents per 14-milligram tablet, or $81 for a 90-day supply. The plan paid $10,239, a 12,403% markup [FvXAV4cqPRg) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (@ 00:02:29]. Pramod John benchmarks the same drug at $28.40 through Cost Plus against roughly $10,000 under the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (plan, a gap of about 300 times [jpLEKhmPpLs @ 00:24:16]. For an operator, that arithmetic is the audit. When one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (molecule shows acquisition cost, transparent retail price and plan-paid price that far apart, the plan has the exact fact) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (pattern plaintiffs are now pleading. Generic and specialty definitions in the PBM contract decide which of those three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (prices the plan ends up paying.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (On the vendor side, John Barl on The Alliance webinar gives the most granular procurement script. Send the RFP to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (three to six vendors and allow about a month for responses. Summarize the responses in a spreadsheet for a benefits) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (committee to review. Review template contracts from the three finalists, score each vendor on a 1-to-10 scale, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (write down why the winner was chosen [2VQyGj0Z_oY @ 00:37:33]. His negotiating benchmarks are specific.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (Typical liability caps run $50K per error, $1M per claim, or four times the last 12 months of fees, and he treats those as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (the starting ranges to argue from [2VQyGj0Z_oY @ 00:38:42]. On term length, he accepts a one-year lock-in followed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (by 60 to 90 days' termination for convenience, and he calls a five-year lock-in risky [2VQyGj0Z_oY @ 00:39:37].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (Frier Levitt's fiduciary checklist covers the PBM side of the same desk. Send a CAA letter demanding consultant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (compensation, audit rebates and spread pricing, and review the formulary and MAC pricing [jpLEKhmPpLs @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (00:44:54]. Each step leaves a dated record: a scored spreadsheet, finalist contract redlines, a compensation letter, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (audit report. Together they turn the abstract prudence duty into a file of evidence. That file shows a process, which is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (what the Seyfarth and Alliance speakers keep returning to as the core of any health plan defense.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (The third mechanic is data, and the speakers agree that sponsors work blind without it. Pramod John says PBMs refuse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (to give plans their own data. That is why his action steps start with getting item-level pricing, then allowing fills at Cost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (Plus and other pharmacies, hiring a non-conflicted consultant, and exploring transparent models [jpLEKhmPpLs @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (00:47:45]. Self Insured Reporting sells the plumbing for that work. It offers more than 100 TPA and PBM integrations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (and loads a plan's data in under a week, so the sponsor is not waiting on a vendor to send reports [Ci7LnsZjk2g @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (00:00:52]. The AHealthcareZ presenter teaches how to read the output. Decide what you want to see first, then look at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (claimants rather than claims, by quarter or year. 5% of members drive 50% of costs at more than $100K each, and 20%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.67 Tm (drive 80% at more than $20K, so the intervention sweet spot is the $20K-$100K band [UQkzQUPP8JE @ 00:02:00].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.45 Tm (In a 100-employee plan spending $1M, that means five people spend about $500K and fifteen people about $300K. His) Tj ET
